        "t": "chr",
        "v": [
          "This module assesses whether the paper's code could be run on its data, and — because `execute = TRUE` — **actually ran it**. We examined 2 R code files.",
          "#### Run order",
          "The scripts were ordered by their data dependencies (a script writing a file another reads runs first), `source()` calls, and numeric filename prefixes.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(Order = 1:2, File = c(\"01_prep.R\", \"02_analysis.R\"\n), \"Runs after\" = c(\"—\", \"01_prep.R\"), Basis = c(\"numeric\", \n\"dependency\")), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### File paths",
          "To run against the Psych-DS layout, 1 referenced data path would be rewritten to its new location.",
          "#### Missing inputs",
          "1 input file the code reads is not available. Files withheld only because of their size are distinguished from files absent from the repository — the former are a size-cap issue, not a reproducibility failure.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = \"not_shared.csv\", Status = \"absent\", Reason = \"referenced file is not present in the repository\"), row.names = c(NA, \n-1L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 10, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "#### Execution",
          "**The code was run.** Each script ran in an isolated subprocess against a throwaway copy of the Psych-DS layout, in the run order above, with a 60-second per-script timeout. Of 2 scripts: 1 ran without error, 0 errored, 0 timed out, 1 was skipped (inputs unavailable), 0 could not run because one of its own dependencies is unavailable, and 0 did not parse. Running against current package versions: a break can reflect version drift, which argues for pinning versions.",
          "\n```{r}\n#| echo: false\n\n\n# table data --------------------------------------\ntable <- structure(list(File = c(\"01_prep.R\", \"02_analysis.R\"), Outcome = c(\"ran_ok\", \n\"skipped_missing_inputs\"), Detail = c(\"\", \"\"), \"Time (s)\" = 0), row.names = c(NA, -2L), class = \"data.frame\")\n\n# display table -----------------------------------\nmetacheck::report_table(table, \"auto\", 15, FALSE)\n```\n",
          "*Expand a row below to see the output each script produced.*",
          "::: {.callout-tip title=\"Output — 01_prep.R (ran_ok)\" collapse=\"true\"}\n\n**Output (stdout):**\n````\n> raw <- read.csv(\"data/study-rawdata_data.csv\")\n> clean <- raw[!is.na(raw$score), ]\n> write.csv(clean,\"<root>/output/clean_data.csv\", row.names = FALSE)\n````\n\n:::\n"
        ]
